-- title:
--   Stabiliser of an elliptic Weierstrass curve as unit group
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field and let $k$ be a field equipped with an $F$-algebra structure which is algebraically closed, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$ which is elliptic (its discriminant is a unit, as recorded by `W.IsElliptic`). Consider the group $\mathrm{VariableChange}\ F$ of admissible changes of variables $(u,r,s,t)$ with $u \in F^\times$, acting on Weierstrass curves over $F$, and let $\mathrm{MulAction.stabilizer}$ denote the stabiliser of $W$ for this action, i.e. the subgroup of those $\gamma$ with $\gamma \bullet W = W$. On the other side, consider the ring $\mathrm{AddMonoid.End}$ of additive endomorphisms of the group of affine points of the base change of $W$ to $k$, and inside it the subring [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring k W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) defined as the subring generated by [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet k W W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28), the set of those additive endomorphisms $\alpha$ that are either zero or satisfy the predicate `IsRationallyRepresented k W W`; let $(\cdot)^\times$ be its group of units. The theorem asserts that the type of group isomorphisms between the stabiliser of $W$ and this unit group is nonempty, i.e. that the two groups are isomorphic; no particular isomorphism is named in the statement.
--
--   This is the classical identification $\mathrm{Aut}_F(W,O) \cong \mathrm{End}_F(W)^\times$ of the automorphism group of a pointed elliptic curve with the units of its endomorphism ring, here with endomorphisms read as additive maps on $k$-points that are rationally represented over $F$. It is used in the computation of widths of places on modular curves, being cited by [`ModularCurve.two_mul_placeWidth_eq_natCard_rationalAut_map_eq_of_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.two_mul_placeWidth_eq_natCard_rationalAut_map_eq_of_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace) and its prime-characteristic variant.
